        "other_parliamentary_business": [
            {
                "body": "The Government has responded to a public (paper) petition calling for reform the NHS dental contract to encourage more dentists to provide NHS care and adopt flexible commissioning to better meet patients\u2019 needs, particularly in coastal areas. The petition was presented to the House of Commons by Steve Darling MP on behalf of residents of the United Kingdom.\n\n* Read the petition and the Government's response[1]\n\nThe petition asks the House of Commons to urge the Government to reform the NHS dental contract to encourage more dentists to provide NHS care and adopt flexible commissioning to better meet patients\u2019 needs, particularly in coastal areas.\n\nIn response to the petition's request, the Government states that since July 2024, the Government has taken steps to strengthen NHS dentistry, delivering nearly 3 million more dental treatments in 2025-26 than before the 2024 election, reducing underspend from \u00a3392 million in 2023-24 to \u00a336 million in 2024-25, and providing 4 million urgent dental appointments, the highest under the current contract. Recognising ongoing access challenges, particularly in rural and coastal areas, the Government has introduced NHS dental contract reforms that prioritise patients with the greatest need, support prevention and complex care, and require urgent care provision. It has also committed to further reform, including a minimum NHS service period for newly qualified dentists and the creation of 50 additional dental school places at Portsmouth and the University of East Anglia, with the aim of improving access to NHS dental services.\n\nWhat are public (paper) petitions?\n\nA public (paper) petition is a petition to the House of Commons presented by an MP.\n\n* Find out more about public (paper) petitions[2]\n\nGet involved in the work of the UK Parliament\n\nYou can also sign up[3] to the UK Parliament newsletter for the latest information on how to get involved and make a difference.\n\n[1]: https://hansard.parliament.uk/Commons/2026-10-13/debates/26101377000029/DentistryInCoastalAreas\n[2]: https://www.parliament.uk/get-involved/sign-a-petition/paper-petitions/\n[3]: https://parliament.us14.list-manage.com/subscribe?u=098af33234df9814f59fb205f&id=6e29cb1262",
                "created_at": "2026-11-03T16:15:12.715Z",
